# capture.py session: Deuteros from a cold boot to the first game screen, two shots.
#   python tools/capture.py --game deuteros --script games/deuteros/scripts/boot.dbg
# Colour counts are those of docs/format.md, "Screens". The title waits for a click and the
# language menu for a key. The data-disk prompt prints a character at a time, so the key and
# the swap come after a long wait. F9 inserts Disk 2 into DF0 (oracle.fsuae.in). WinUAE swaps
# with the debugger command `I floppy0=<Disk 2 path>` instead, which this script has not been
# run with. A key sent less than 3 s after the swap is missed.
!until 16
!sleep 3
!click
!until 4
!sleep 1
!shot language-menu
!key 1 0.2
!sleep 12
!key f9 0.2
!sleep 3
!key space 0.2
!until 18
!sleep 1
!shot earth-base
